msgstr "Ang problemang phase estimation"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"
msgstr "Ang problemang phase estimation {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section of the lesson explains the *phase estimation problem*.\n"
"We'll begin with a short discussion of the *spectral theorem* from linear algebra, and then move on to a statement of the phase estimation problem itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapaliwanag ng seksyong ito ng aralin ang *problemang phase estimation*.\n"
"Magsisimula tayo sa maikling talakayan ng *spectral theorem* mula sa linear algebra, tapos lilipat tayo sa pagsasaad ng problemang phase estimation mismo.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *spectral theorem* is an important fact from linear algebra that states that matrices of a certain type, called *normal matrices,* can be expressed in a simple and useful way.\n"
"We'll only need this theorem for unitary matrices in this lesson, but down the road in this series we'll apply it to Hermitian matrices as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang *spectral theorem* ay isang mahalagang katotohanan mula sa linear algebra na nagsasaad na ang mga matrix ng isang tiyak na uri, na tinatawag na *normal matrices,* ay maaaring ipahayag sa isang simple at kapaki-pakinabang na paraan.\n"
"Kakailanganin lang natin ang theorem na ito para sa mga unitary matrix sa araling ito, ngunit sa susunod na bahagi ng seryeng ito ay ilalapat din natin ito sa mga Hermitian matrix.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal matrices {#normal-matrices}"
msgstr "Mga normal matrix {#normal-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $M$ with complex number entries is said to be a *normal* matrix if it commutes with its conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang square matrix $M$ na may mga complex number na entry ay tinatawag na *normal* matrix kung ito ay commute sa kanyang conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every unitary matrix $U$ is normal because\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat unitary matrix $U$ ay normal dahil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hermitian matrices, which are matrices that equal their own conjugate transpose, are another important class of normal matrices.\n"
"If $H$ is a Hermitian matrix, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga Hermitian matrix, na mga matrix na katumbas ng kanilang sariling conjugate transpose, ay isa pang mahalagang klase ng mga normal matrix.\n"
"Kung ang $H$ ay isang Hermitian matrix, kung gayon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so $H$ is normal.\n"
msgstr "kaya normal ang $H$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every square matrix is normal.\n"
"For instance, this matrix isn't normal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi lahat ng square matrix ay normal.\n"
"Halimbawa, hindi normal ang matrix na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(This is a simple but great example of a matrix that's often very helpful to consider.)\n"
"It isn't normal because\n"
msgstr ""
"(Ito ay isang simple ngunit napakagandang halimbawa ng matrix na madalas na napakatulong isaalang-alang.)\n"
"Hindi ito normal dahil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "while\n"
msgstr "habang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement {#theorem-statement}"
msgstr "Pahayag ng theorem {#theorem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now here's a statement of the spectral theorem.\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang pahayag ng spectral theorem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a normal $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $N$-dimensional complex vectors $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Hayaan ang $M$ na maging isang normal na $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"May umiiral na orthonormal basis ng $N$-dimensional complex vectors na $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ kasama ang mga complex number na $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ na nagpapatunay na\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The expression of a matrix in the form\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapahayag ng matrix sa anyong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is commonly called a *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Notice that if $M$ is a normal matrix expressed in the form $(1)$, then the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"ay karaniwang tinatawag na *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Pansinin na kung ang $M$ ay isang normal matrix na naipahayag sa anyong $(1)$, kung gayon ang ekwasyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"must be true for every $j = 1,\\ldots,N$.\n"
"This is a consequence of the fact that $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ is orthonormal:\n"
msgstr ""
"ay dapat na totoo para sa bawat $j = 1,\\ldots,N$.\n"
"Ito ay bunga ng katotohanan na ang $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ ay orthonormal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, each number $\\lambda_j$ is an *eigenvalue* of $M$ and $\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* corresponding to that eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr "Ibig sabihin, ang bawat numero na $\\lambda_j$ ay isang *eigenvalue* ng $M$ at ang $\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ ay isang *eigenvector* na naaayon sa eigenvalue na iyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.\n"
"Let\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Halimbawa 1**.\n"
"Hayaan\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  which is normal.\n"
"  The theorem implies that $\\mathbb{I}$ can be written in the form $(1)$ for some choice of $\\lambda_1$, $\\lambda_2$, $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$, and $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle$.\n"
"  There are multiple choices that work, including\n"
msgstr ""
"  na normal.\n"
"  Ipinahihiwatig ng theorem na ang $\\mathbb{I}$ ay maaaring isulat sa anyong $(1)$ para sa ilang pagpili ng $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ at $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  Mayroong maraming pagpili na gumagana, kasama na ang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Notice that the theorem does not say that the complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ are\n"
"  distinct — we can have the same complex number repeated, which is necessary for this example.\n"
"  These choices work because\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pansinin na hindi sinasabi ng theorem na ang mga complex number na $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ ay\n"
"  natatangi — maaari tayong magkaroon ng parehong complex number na paulit-ulit, na kinakailangan para sa halimbawang ito.\n"
"  Gumagana ang mga pagpiling ito dahil\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Indeed, we could choose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ to be *any* orthonormal basis and the\n"
"  equation will be true. For instance,\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa katunayan, maaari nating piliin ang $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ na maging *anumang* orthonormal basis at\n"
"  magiging totoo ang ekwasyon. Halimbawa,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 2**.\n"
"Consider a Hadamard operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Halimbawa 2**.\n"
"Isaalang-alang ang isang Hadamard operation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is a unitary matrix, so it is normal. The spectral theorem implies that $H$ can be written in the\n"
"  form $(1)$, and in particular we have\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ito ay isang unitary matrix, kaya ito ay normal. Ipinahihiwatig ng spectral theorem na ang $H$ ay maaaring isulat sa\n"
"  anyong $(1)$, at partikular na mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  where\n"
msgstr "  kung saan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  More explicitly,\n"
msgstr "  Mas malinaw,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  We can check that this decomposition is correct by performing the required calculations:\n"
msgstr "  Maaari nating suriin na tama ang decomposition na ito sa pamamagitan ng pagsasagawa ng mga kinakailangang kalkulasyon:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the first example above reveals, there can be some freedom in how eigenvectors are selected.\n"
"There is, however, no freedom at all in how the eigenvalues are chosen, except for their ordering:\n"
"the same $N$ complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$, which can include repetitions of the same complex number, will always occur in the equation $(1)$ for a given choice of a matrix $M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng ipinapakita ng unang halimbawa sa itaas, maaaring may kalayaan sa kung paano pinipili ang mga eigenvector.\n"
"Walang kalayaan, gayunpaman, sa kung paano pinipili ang mga eigenvalue, maliban sa kanilang pagkakasunod-sunod:\n"
"ang parehong $N$ complex number na $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$, na maaaring magsama ng mga paulit-ulit na parehong complex number, ay laging lilitaw sa ekwasyong $(1)$ para sa isang ibinigay na pagpili ng matrix na $M$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's focus in on unitary matrices.\n"
"Suppose we have a complex number $\\lambda$ and a non-zero vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, tumuon tayo sa mga unitary matrix.\n"
"Ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong complex number na $\\lambda$ at isang hindi-zero na vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ na nagpapatunay sa ekwasyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $U$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector corresponding to this eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr "Ibig sabihin, ang $\\lambda$ ay isang eigenvalue ng $U$ at ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay isang eigenvector na naaayon sa eigenvalue na ito.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unitary matrices preserve Euclidean norm, and so we conclude the following from $(2)$.\n"
msgstr "Pinapanatili ng mga unitary matrix ang Euclidean norm, kaya naman nakukuha natin ang sumusunod mula sa $(2)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The condition that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is non-zero implies that $\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0$, so we can cancel it from both sides to obtain\n"
msgstr "Ang kondisyon na ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay hindi-zero ay nangangahulugang $\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0$, kaya maaari nating kanselahin ito mula sa magkabilang panig upang makuha\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This reveals that eigenvalues of unitary matrices must always have absolute value equal to one, so they lie on the *unit circle.*\n"
msgstr "Ibinubunyag nito na ang mga eigenvalue ng mga unitary matrix ay palaging may absolute value na katumbas ng isa, kaya nasa *unit circle* sila.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The symbol $\\mathbb{T}$ is a common name for the complex unit circle. The name $S^1$ is also common.)\n"
msgstr "(Ang simbolong $\\mathbb{T}$ ay isang karaniwang pangalan para sa complex unit circle. Karaniwang ginagamit din ang pangalang $S^1$.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase estimation problem statement {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"
msgstr "Pahayag ng problemang phase estimation {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the *phase estimation problem*, we're given a quantum state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of $n$ qubits, along with a unitary quantum circuit that acts on $n$ qubits.\n"
"We're *promised* that $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of the unitary matrix $U$ that describes the action of the circuit, and our goal is to compute or approximate the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ to which $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ corresponds.\n"
"More precisely, because $\\lambda$ lies on the complex unit circle, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa *problemang phase estimation*, binibigyan tayo ng quantum state na $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ ng $n$ qubits, kasama ang isang unitary quantum circuit na kumikilos sa $n$ qubits.\n"
"*Ipinangako* na ang $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ ay isang eigenvector ng unitary matrix na $U$ na naglalarawan sa aksyon ng circuit, at ang ating layunin ay kalkulahin o tantiyahin ang eigenvalue na $\\lambda$ na naaayon sa $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Mas tiyak, dahil ang $\\lambda$ ay nasa complex unit circle, maaari nating isulat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a unique real number $\\theta$ satisfying $0\\leq\\theta<1$.\n"
"The goal of the problem is to compute or approximate this real number $\\theta$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa isang natatanging real number na $\\theta$ na nagpapatunay ng $0\\leq\\theta<1$.\n"
"Ang layunin ng problema ay kalkulahin o tantiyahin ang real number na $\\theta$ na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Phase estimation problem\">\n"
"Input: A unitary quantum circuit for an $n$-qubit operation $U$ along with an $n$-qubit quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promise: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U$ \\\n"
"Output: an approximation to the number $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfying $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problemang phase estimation\">\n"
"Input: Isang unitary quantum circuit para sa isang $n$-qubit operation na $U$ kasama ang isang $n$-qubit quantum state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Pangako: Ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay isang eigenvector ng $U$ \\\n"
"Output: isang pagtatantya sa numero na $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ na nagpapatunay ng $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few remarks about this problem statement:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang ilang mga puna tungkol sa pahayag ng problemang ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem is different from other problems we've seen so far in the course in that the input includes a quantum state. Typically we focus on problems having classical inputs and outputs, but nothing prevents us from considering quantum state inputs like this. In terms of its practical relevance, the phase estimation problem is typically encountered as a *subproblem* inside of a larger computation, like we'll see in the context of integer factorization later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr "Ang problemang phase estimation ay naiiba sa iba pang mga problema na nakita natin sa kurso dahil ang input ay nagsasama ng quantum state. Karaniwan ay nakatutok tayo sa mga problemang may classical na input at output, ngunit walang pumipigil sa atin na isaalang-alang ang mga quantum state input tulad nito. Sa mga tuntunin ng praktikal na kaugnayan, ang problemang phase estimation ay karaniwang nararatagpuan bilang isang *subproblem* sa loob ng isang mas malaking computation, tulad ng makikita natin sa konteksto ng integer factorization sa susunod na bahagi ng aralin.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The statement of the phase estimation problem above isn't specific about what constitutes an approximation of $\\theta$, but we can formulate more precise problem statements depending on our needs and interests. In the context of integer factorization, we'll demand a very precise approximation to $\\theta$, but in other cases we might be satisfied with a very rough approximation. We'll discuss shortly how the precision we require affects the computational cost of a solution.\n"
msgstr "Ang pahayag ng problemang phase estimation sa itaas ay hindi tiyak tungkol sa kung ano ang bumubuo ng pagtatantya ng $\\theta$, ngunit maaari tayong bumuo ng mas tumpak na mga pahayag ng problema depende sa ating mga pangangailangan at interes. Sa konteksto ng integer factorization, mangangailangan tayo ng napaka-tumpak na pagtatantya ng $\\theta$, ngunit sa ibang mga kaso maaaring masaya na tayo sa isang magaspang na pagtatantya. Tatalakayin natin sa ilang sandali kung paano nakakaapekto ang katumpakang kailangan natin sa computational cost ng isang solusyon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice that as we go from $\\theta = 0$ toward $\\theta = 1$ in the phase estimation problem, we're going all the way around the unit circle, starting from $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ and moving counter-clockwise toward $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1$. That is, when we reach $\\theta = 1$ we're back where we started at $\\theta = 0$. So, as we consider the accuracy of approximations, choices of $\\theta$ near $1$ should be considered as being near $0$. For example, an approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ should be considered as being within $1/1000$ of $\\theta = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin na habang tumatahak tayo mula sa $\\theta = 0$ patungo sa $\\theta = 1$ sa problemang phase estimation, umiikot tayo nang buo sa unit circle, simula sa $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ at gumagalaw counter-clockwise patungo sa $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1$. Ibig sabihin, kapag naabot natin ang $\\theta = 1$ ay nandoon na tayo uli sa $\\theta = 0$. Kaya, habang isinasaalang-alang natin ang katumpakan ng mga pagtatantya, ang mga pagpili ng $\\theta$ malapit sa $1$ ay dapat ituring na malapit sa $0$. Halimbawa, ang pagtatantya na $\\theta = 0.999$ ay dapat ituring na nasa loob ng $1/1000$ ng $\\theta = 0$.\n"
